      187.29,
      228.53,
      376.41,
      252.47
    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE PRIMARY COURT\u2019S PROCEDUREACT, NO. OF 1979",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      266.33,
      401.9,
      290.27
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      304.13,
      401.78,
      328.07
    ],
    "text": "1. This Act may be cited as the Primary Court\u2019s Procedure(Amendment) Act, No. of 2024.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      341.93,
      401.89,
      391.07
    ],
    "text": "2. The following new sections are hereby insertedimmediately after section 70 of the Primary Court\u2019s ProcedureAct, No. 44 of 1979 and shall have effect as sections 70Aand 70B of that enactment: -",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      404.93,
      401.88,
      441.47
    ],
    "text": "70A. (1) Where at the time the Judge of thePrimary Court delivers an order, under section68 or 69, as the case may be-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      221.85,
      455.33,
      401.86,
      504.47
    ],
    "text": "(a) if, any party to the dispute asspecified in paragraph (b) ofsubsection (1) of section 66, makesan application; or",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      237.57,
      518.33,
      401.87,
      580.07
    ],
    "text": "(b)if, the Judge of the Primary Court isof the opinion that the matter indispute is related to a title or interestof a party, and it is appropriate to beadjudicated by a District Court,",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      593.93,
      401.89,
      670.67
    ],
    "text": "the Judge of the Primary Court shall direct theRegistrar to forward the case record to theDistrict Court having jurisdiction of the landor right or interest to the land in disputesituates, while keeping a copy of the order,within one month from the date of the order.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      407.85,
      305.11,
      443.85,
      314.18
    ],
    "text": "Short title",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
