  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      166.97,
      360.31,
      178.31
    ],
    "text": "2Primary Court\u2019s Procedure (Amendment)",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      212.11,
      203.69,
      398.27,
      306.71
    ],
    "text": "(2) Notwithstanding an order to forward thecase record to the District Court, the Judge ofthe Primary Court may direct the parties toexecute any order made by him within onemonth from the date of such order and issuefurther orders on the parties to maintain thestatus quo until any order, whether interim orfinal, is made by the District Court.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      212.11,
      321.65,
      398.13,
      385.31
    ],
    "text": "(3) Notwithstanding the provisions of anyother law, no appeal or revision shall lie againstany order of the Judge of the Primary Court,from the date on which he made an order toforward the case record to the District Court.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      212.11,
      400.25,
      398.23,
      463.91
    ],
    "text": "70B. (1) Upon receipt of a case record undersection 70A, the judge of the District Court shallallocate a case number and issue notice on theparties to appear before the Court on a date notlater than one month from the date of such order.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      212.11,
      478.73,
      398.16,
      555.59
    ],
    "text": "(2) The District Court shall proceed withthe matter as if such matter has been institutedunder the Chapter XLIII of the Civil ProcedureCode (Chapter 101) and the provisions thereofshall mutatis mutandis apply in relation to suchproceedings.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      212.11,
      570.53,
      398.14,
      673.55
    ],
    "text": "(3) The District Court shall order the partiesto submit their statements of claims. TheDistrict Court may, on its\u2019 own motion or onan application by any party before it, add anyother party to the proceedings, if the court is ofthe opinion that such addition may benecessary for the ends of justice or to preventabuse of the process of the Court.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      140.11,
      257.09,
      145.11,
      268.43
    ],
