  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      198.57,
      166.97,
      401.69,
      178.31
    ],
    "text": "Primary Court\u2019s Procedure (Amendment)3",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      204.65,
      401.87,
      281.51
    ],
    "text": "(4) The District Court, on an application ofa party or on its\u2019 own motion, and if the court issatisfied, may set-aside, vary, alter or amendany order made by the Judge of the PrimaryCourt under section 70A, at any stage beforethe final judgment is pronounced.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      296.45,
      401.87,
      373.19
    ],
    "text": "(5) Where this Act has not provided for anymatter arising in such proceedings, theprovisions of the Civil Procedure Code(Chapter 101) governing a like matter shall,with suitable adaptation as the justice of thecase may require be adopted and applied.\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      388.13,
      401.89,
      412.55
    ],
    "text": "3. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.",
